1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,279
Here is a quick tour of your updated Courtside interface.

2
00:00:04,339 --> 00:00:08,632
The goal was to make it feel professional and easier to use on a phone.

3
00:00:08,692 --> 00:00:13,691
These screens use sample sessions, so the measurements are illustrations.

4
00:00:14,391 --> 00:00:21,804
First, the desktop layout has a consistent green and warm white theme, clearer headings, and a simpler sidebar.

5
00:00:21,864 --> 00:00:28,262
The main pages are Live Court, Overview, Session Library, My Progress, and Coaching Notes.

6
00:00:28,322 --> 00:00:32,036
Settings and release checks sit in the workspace section.

7
00:00:32,736 --> 00:00:37,110
On a phone, the header gives the workspace selector its own row.

8
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:41,544
Page names stay readable, and buttons have more room to tap.

9
00:00:41,604 --> 00:00:49,222
The session library lets you search, filter by type or status, and switch between cards and a compact list.

10
00:00:49,282 --> 00:00:53,521
In list view, the status sits below each session title.

11
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:58,804
Live Court puts the camera preview first and the setup panel below it.

12
00:00:58,864 --> 00:01:03,168
Choose a camera and confirm processing permission before starting.

13
00:01:03,228 --> 00:01:08,786
If a junior is present, guardian consent and player agreement are also required.

14
00:01:08,846 --> 00:01:12,140
The camera stays off until you start the feed.

15
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:16,079
Open a session to review individual shots.

16
00:01:16,139 --> 00:01:20,438
On a phone, the shot picker comes before the selected shot.

17
00:01:20,498 --> 00:01:25,366
All shot filters remain visible, and the list scrolls within its panel.

18
00:01:25,426 --> 00:01:30,685
The report then shows the clip, technique measurements, and coaching observations.

19
00:01:31,385 --> 00:01:34,774
My Progress compares your sessions over time.

20
00:01:34,834 --> 00:01:39,148
The chart adapts to the screen width while keeping its labels readable.

21
00:01:39,208 --> 00:01:45,616
Upload dialogs also fit the phone screen, and their close button stays visible while you scroll.

22
00:01:46,316 --> 00:01:51,439
Finally, the menu works on both portrait and short landscape screens.

23
00:01:51,499 --> 00:01:58,068
The main pages were checked on phone and tablet sizes, and all twenty six frontend tests passed.

24
00:01:58,128 --> 00:02:05,131
Start in the session library to explore the examples, or open Live Court when you are ready to set up a session.
